  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Hu Immortal blessed land is an enslavement path immortal aperture, and Fang Yuan’s strength path immortal aperture is dead. Both have sparse soul path dao marks, so even if he wanted to, he could not raise white lotus giant silkworm Gu to feed cleanse soul Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        852
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_white_lotus_giant_silkworm_gu",
        "gu_cleanse_soul"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "General dao marks and attainment levels are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nether grass is a desolate plant that contains large numbers of soul path dao marks. As time passes, it influences the surroundings so a wide range becomes a breeding ground for soul path Gu worms, and it can modify a blessed land or grotto-heaven environment.",
      "chapters": [
        909
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "nether-grass-breeding-ground",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "res_nether_grass",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Desolate plants as a tier are covered on desolate plant.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "nether-grass-breeding-ground",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_desolate_plant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Secluded domains of heaven and earth are usually mysterious. Dang Hun Mountain and Luo Po Valley are filled with soul path dao marks, while Ascending Heaven Plain has an uncountable number of space path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        986
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "secluded-domains",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_dang_hun_mountain",
        "loc_luo_po_valley",
        "loc_ascending_heaven_plain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Guts Gu and Luo Po winds are, in essence, ways of adding soul path dao marks to Fang Yuan’s soul.",
      "chapters": [
        1482
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "secluded-domains",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_guts_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan does not cultivate soul path. Soul path Gu Immortals have soul path dao marks which allow the body to hold an even stronger soul. Immortal zombie bodies can contain souls past a living body’s ordinary limit, but they lack the living body’s nourishing aspect, so guts Gu and other soul path methods matter for keeping a large soul intact.",
      "chapters": [
        997
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "holding-a-stronger-soul",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "path_soul",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "res_immortal_zombie_corpse"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During his battle against Heaven Overseeing Tower, more than half the soul path dao marks on Spectral Soul Demon Venerable’s body are already gone, and the rest still shine on him as thick as a sky of stars.",
      "chapters": [
        1018
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "depleted-but-still-shining",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower",
        "char_spectral_soul_demon_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Soul beasts nurture a soul core the size of an egg that holds a large number of soul path dao marks and is treated as a top tier refinement material. After death the rest of the corpse fades and has no further use.",
      "chapters": [
        1042
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-beasts",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_soul_beast"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A portion of soul beasts form naturally in places with dense soul path dao marks, after Red Lotus Demon Venerable damaged fate Gu and Spectral Soul Demon Venerable created soul path.",
      "chapters": [
        1503
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-beasts",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable",
        "gu_fate_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Even at hundred million man soul, Fang Yuan’s soul had few soul path dao marks because Dang Hun Mountain and Luo Po Valley built foundation without the usual mark accumulation. Breaking through to desolate soul pushes the soul path dao marks on that soul past ten thousand.",
      "chapters": [
        1804
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "few-marks-despite-foundation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the five regions and two heavens, living beings have souls because of soul path dao marks. A small world without those marks can hold living beings that have no souls at all.",
      "chapters": [
        1867
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "living-beings-and-souls",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soul Pacifying grotto-heaven holds over seven million soul path dao marks, most accumulated as generations of Gu Immortals merge apertures rather than from tribulations alone. Dense soul path dao marks give a natural advantage for soul path cultivation and resources inside that grotto-heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        2078
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grotto-heaven-accumulation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_soul_pacifying_grotto_heaven"
      ]
    }
  ],
